 "amendments": {
  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend chapter 497 of the laws of 2016 amending the education law\nrelating to the licensure of pathologists' assistants, in relation to the\neffectiveness thereof",
    "basePrintNo": "S8088",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S8088-2017",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §2, Chap 497 of 2016",
    "lawSection": "Education",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S8088\n\nSPONSOR: LAVALLE\n \nTITLE OF BILL:  An act to amend chapter 497 of the laws of 2016 amend-\ning the education law relating to the licensure of pathologists' assist-\nants, in relation to the effectiveness thereof\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThis bill would amend the effective date of licensure for pathologists'\nassistants.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1. Amends the effective date of Section 2 of Chapter 497 of the\nLaws of 2016 to July 1, 2018.\n\nSection 2. Provides that the bill is effective immediately.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nIn 2016, the Legislature passed and Governor Cuomo signed legislation\n(Chapter 497 of the Laws of 2016) creating a new licensure category for\npathologists' assistants. The current effective date for section 8852 of\nthe education law is two years after enactment, November 28, 2018.\nHowever, another provision of the education law that currently permits\nthese individuals to practice under a limited license will expire on\nSeptember 1, 2018 thus creating at a minimum an unintended licensure gap\nbetween these two dates.\n\nThe initial two-year effective date was meant to provide the State\nEducation Department (SED) with sufficient time to establish the mech-\nanism for processing new applications which was expected to begin in the\nsummer of 2018. However, because the bill was not signed into law until\nNovember 28, 2016, the two-year period effectively became two and one\nhalf years and created the above referenced gap. Amending the effective\ndate to July 1, 2018 fixes this issue.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nImmediately\n",
